# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on a Windows checkout.
#
# Several tests read this repository's own source as text — the generator surface count,
# the locale-module/manifest agreement checks — and Swift's Character is an extended
# grapheme cluster, so CRLF is a *single* Character. Splitting on "\n" therefore finds no
# separators at all on a CRLF checkout and returns the whole file as one line. The tests
# are newline-agnostic now, but normalising here removes the class rather than the instance.
#
# It also keeps the corpus adapters honest: several parse pinned upstream text files, and a
# checkout that rewrote their bytes would change what the integrity hashes are computed over.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.decoy      binary
*.xlsx       binary
*.zip        binary
*.png        binary
*.ico        binary
